A||||4||Spektyr||Chattering Heat shield||||1||
Z||000000||Spektyr||05-10-2001||10:26 AM||||Okay, even though my 85GT is running rich a little bit smokey at WOT, and generally making me a little worried, the chattering heatshield is what is bothering me the most.<P>It's the one that runs across the back of the motor (that's the back of the motor, not the car, non-belt or drivers side of car).  Runs from one side of the motor to the other, right under the throttle body and EGR valve.  The side right under the throttle body is loose, and I can't really see up under there to figure out where it's supposed to connect, and for all my feeling around, I can't seem to find the hole the missing bolt goes through.<P>So here's the question: where does the bolt go, and what bolt do I need to replace the missing one?  I can't find this anywhere in my Haynes manual, it only mentions the heatshields when they need to be removed to get at something.  ie. 'Remove the heatshield to allow access too...'  It never mentions where the heck the bolts are, and I haven't found any pictures to help me out.<P>I'm about to just take something and tie it around the shield and throttle body to hold it up where it won't rattle.  It doesn't really sound like valve train noise, but the chattering is close enough it makes me paranoid.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||05-10-2001||01:11 PM||||You say it runs from one side to the other on an '85 GT under the throttle body?<BR>Are you trying to say it's over the cross over pipe?<BR>If so, from rear to front, there should be a sheet metal screw beside the coil holding the shield from the coil to the first section of the exhaust shield. (points down) Then, joining the two halves of the exhaust shields together under the EGR valve, one goes in from the right SIDE (at the distributor) and another opposite from that. Toward the front of the car, the lower attaching point is at the bell housing bolt (the one that holds the transmission to the engine).<BR>Hope this helps you.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||05-10-2001||01:14 PM||||What usually happens with these is the vibration pulls the shield away from the bolt head...the bolt head is usually still there beneath the shield (pull it away and look).<P>Once you find where the bolts go, be sure to place a washer under the new bolt so it won't pull out again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spektyr||05-10-2001||06:12 PM||||Okay, I just went out and checked my heat shield.  It's not connected at the bell housing side, all the other screws are in place.  I felt all along everywhere I could find and found no evidence of a bolt, or anywhere a bolt would fit through the shield.  It feels as though there just isn't anywhere to put a bolt through that end of the shield.<P>I'm just about to fix it with some bailing wire...||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTZ34||05-10-2001||10:35 PM||||There are a set of 'ears' or tabs that make a right angle to the top of the shield, and are part of the shield itself.  These ears are parallel to the back of the motor.  One of the bellhousing bolts (top left as you look at the back of the motor) is a studbolt and the ears fit on there and a nut holds it in place.  If that is missing I'll bet you do have a rattle...||||reg||1
